    "Pagaste %@ %@ (%@). ¿Lo registramos este mes? Mantén presionado para responder si fue el mismo monto u otro.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid %@ %@ (%@). Should we log it this month? Press and hold to answer whether it was the same amount or a different one."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste en %@ 💳": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid at %@ 💳"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@ — eso alcanza para completar tu meta \"%@\" %@. ¿Lo aportamos?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left — that's enough to complete your goal \"%@\" %@. Want to contribute it?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@ — un sobrante grande. Antes de invertirlo, confirma que ya cubres de 3 a 6 meses de gastos en tu fondo de emergencia; si ya los tienes, este es buen momento para ponerlo a trabajar.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left — a big surplus. Before investing it, make sure your emergency fund already covers 3 to 6 months of expenses; if it does, this is a great time to put it to work."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@. Antes de ahorrarlo o invertirlo, te conviene abonarlo a tu deuda con %@%@ — ningun ahorro te rinde mas que dejar de pagar esos intereses.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left. Before saving or investing it, you're better off putting it toward your debt with %@%@ — no savings earn you more than ending those interest payments."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@. Buen momento para crear una meta de ahorro en MonAvi — hasta un fondo de emergencia chico te da colchon para el proximo imprevisto.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left. A good time to create a savings goal in MonAvi — even a small emergency fund gives you a cushion for the next surprise."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@. Es poco para invertir, pero es perfecto para empezar tu fondo de emergencia — cada poquito cuenta.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left. It's not much to invest, but it's perfect to start your emergency fund — every little bit counts."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@. Si lo aportas a tu meta \"%@\" %@, llegarias al %@%% — vas en %@%% ahorita.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left. If you contribute it to your goal \"%@\" %@, you'd reach %@%% — you're at %@%% right now."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@. Si ya tienes de 3 a 6 meses de gastos ahorrados, es buen monto para empezar a invertir; si no, te conviene completar ese fondo primero.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left. If you already have 3 to 6 months of expenses saved, this is a good amount to start investing; if not, you're better off completing that fund first."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pagaste tus cuentas y te quedaron %@. Tienes deuda con %@%@ — abonarla rinde mas que cualquier ahorro, pero antes revisa si tu colchon actual te alcanza para imprevistos. Si si, destinalo a la deuda; si no, considera repartirlo entre tu reserva y la deuda.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "You paid your bills and have %@ left. You have debt with %@%@ — paying it down earns you more than any savings, but first check whether your current emergency fund is enough for surprises. If it is, put it toward the debt; if not, consider splitting it between your reserve and the debt."
          }
        }
      }
    },
